From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 01:18:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mailbox: apple,mailbox: Add the T8010 A7 IOP
 mailbox

The coprocessors of the A10 (T8010), such as the GPU coprocessor and the
always-on processor, use an older mailbox than the ASC and M3 variants:
each message is a single 64-bit word, with the endpoint in bits 63:56
and a 56-bit payload. Its four interrupts are the same as those of the
other variants.

Add a compatible for it.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml         | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
index 28985cc..ba035ff 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
@@ -52,6 +52,13 @@ properties:
               - apple,t6000-m3-mailbox
           - const: apple,m3-mailbox-v2
 
+      - description:
+          The A7 IOP mailbox (AppleA7IOP) is an older variant found on the
+          A10, used for example by the GPU and always-on coprocessors. Each
+          message is a single 64-bit word with the endpoint in its top byte.
+        items:
+          - const: apple,t8010-a7iop-mailbox
+
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
-- 
